 tired narrative of black-Asian interracial tension generates heat, but not light. There's a far more complex and nuanced relationship between these two urban populations, one that is in an ongoing state of evolution -- and it deserves to be told, not buried under cliches and clickbait.\\n\",\"answer\":\"On Thursday, NPR broadcast an update on the unrest in Baltimore, Maryland, following the death of 25-year-old Freddie Gray due to spinal injuries sustained while in police custody. However, the report focused on allegations that African Americans were targeting Asian-owned businesses for destruction, perpetuating a harmful and false narrative that has been present in media coverage of similar events since the 1980s. Professors Jennifer Lee and Michael C. Dawson note that the media's tendency to pit minority groups against each other serves to deflect attention from broader structural issues and systemic inequality affecting marginalized communities. While interethnic tensions do exist, the reality is more complex and nuanced, with many storeowners and customers recognizing their shared struggles and working towards mutual understanding and support.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":293},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":293,\"byte_end\":376},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":376,\"byte_end\":754},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":754,\"byte_end\":829},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":829,\"byte_end\":1085},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":1085,\"byte_end\":1183},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":1183,\"byte_end\":1262},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":1262,\"byte_end\":1536},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":1536,\"byte_end\":1745},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":1745,\"byte_end\":1840},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":1840,\"byte_end\":1995},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":1995,\"byte_end\":2341},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":2341,\"byte_end\":2503},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":2503,\"byte_end\":2520},{\"index\":14,\"byte_start\":2520,\"byte_end\":2720},{\"index\":15,\"byte_start\":2720,\"