s briefing on the FSU case, we turned our attention to Jameis and got it filed.\\\" Kinsman also sued the university in January. According to police documents in the rape case, Kinsman said Winston raped her after she had been drinking with friends at a bar in Tallahassee. She said an unknown man gave her a shot glass of liquid before they left the bar. Kinsman also said she did not remember much of what happened next but that she remembered being in a ground-floor apartment, where Winston took off her clothes and had sex with her despite her objections, according to police documents. Kinsman reported the alleged assault to FSU campus police that night. A month later, in January 2013, she told Tallahassee police that Winston was the attacker. Tallahassee's interim police chief at the time, Tom Coe, said the woman \\\"broke off contact\\\" with investigators in February 2013 and didn't want to go forward with the case. The woman's family said a detective warned her attorney that Tallahassee is a \\\"big football town\\\" and that life could be miserable if she pursued the case. Winston didn't play during the 2012 season but came to Florida State as one of the nation's top quarterback recruits, according to recruiting rankings.\\n\",\"answer\":\"Erica Kinsman, a former Florida State University student, has filed a lawsuit against Jameis Winston, a former FSU football player, alleging that he raped her in December 2012. Kinsman has also accused Winston of false imprisonment and intentional infliction of emotional distress. Winston has denied the allegations, saying that the sex was consensual. Kinsman's lawyer, John Clune, stated that the lawsuit was filed now because they did not want to wait until the eve of the NFL draft or after Winston had signed a contract. Winston is expected to be a top pick in the draft, which starts on April 30. Kinsman has also sued FSU in January.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":212},{\"index\":1,\"byte_sta