ence of any clue in both these instances is rare.\\nAdding another dimension to Dulce's case, Steele labeled it as an \\\"old-school disappearance,\\\" referring to the complete absence of technological evidence, which is quite unusual in today's era where many disappearances have online interactions as an underlying factor.\\nDetermined to breathe new life into the investigation, Steele and his team aim to approach Dulce's case from a new angle, relying on fresh perspectives, technologies, and a thorough approach.\\nWhile Spierer's parents, Robert and Charlene, still hope for their daughter's return, they maintain a Facebook page dedicated to her.\\nIn another related development, The National Center for Missing and Exploited Children released an age-progressed picture of Dulce on the fourth anniversary of her disappearance, hoping it might lead to her identification. Dulce's mother, shocked by the progression, expressed how different her daughter looked but noted that her eyes remained unmistakably familiar.\\nThe quest for answers in both cases continues, as families and investigators seek closure.\",\"answer\":\"The unsolved disappearances of Lauren Spierer and Dulce Alavez in New Jersey have raised disturbing similarities, potentially offering crucial leads, according to a private detective. Five-year-old Dulce went missing from a park in 2019, and despite an extensive search, no significant leads have been found. Lauren, a 20-year-old university student, disappeared in 2011. Trent Steele, co-founder of the Anti-Predator Project, noted the lack of any trace in both cases, which is rare for missing person cases. Steele's team plans to approach Dulce's case from a fresh perspective. The National Center for Missing and Exploited Children has released an age-progressed picture of Dulce on the fourth anniversary of her disappearance.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":287},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":287,\"byte_end\":428},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":428,\"byte_end\":522},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":522,\"byte_end\":741},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":741,\"byte_end\":864},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":864,\"byte_end\":957},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":957,\"byte_end\":1086},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":1086,\"byte_end\":1184},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":1184,\"byte_end\":1378},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":1378,\"byte_end\":1565},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":1565,\"byte_end\":1719},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":1719,\"byte_end\":1988},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":1988,\"byte_end\":2180},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":2180,\"byte_end\":2314},{\"index\":14,\"byte_start\":2314,\"byte_end\":2537},{\"index\":15,\"byte_start\":2537,\"byte_end\":2681},{\"index\":16,\"byte_start\":2681,\"byte_end\":2771}],\"answer_sentence_indices\":[0,1,2,3,4],\"answer_offsets\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":184},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":184,\"byte_end\":309},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":309,\"byte_end\":510},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":510,\"byte_end\":581},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":581,\"byte_end\":731}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n", "add_special": true}
