egrees.Place the chicken pieces on a rimmed baking sheet and place it in the oven on rack position 2 (counting up from the bottom of the oven) Cook for 20 minutes, turn the pieces, brush with the BBQ sauce and cook for another 15 minutes.lace the chicken pieces on a rimmed baking sheet and place it in the oven on rack position 2 (counting up from the bottom of the oven) Cook for 20 minutes, turn the pieces, brush with the BBQ sauce and cook for another 15 minutes.\\\\n\\\\npassage 2:You should cook chicken legs in an convection oven for between 20 and 30 minutes depending on the temperature.The air movement of convection ovens greatly reduces cooking times when compared to traditional ovens.ou should cook chicken legs in an convection oven for between 20 and 30 minutes depending on the temperature.\\\\n\\\\npassage 3:Pre-heat oven to Convection Roast 400 degrees. Meanwhile, cover a pan with foil, and spray with a thin layer of canola spray. Place the chicken legs on the foil until the oven is preheated-about 15 minutes. When ready, put the pan in the oven and set your timer for 20 minutes.When time is up, change your heat to 325 degrees, then set timer for 10 minutes. When time is up, remove pan from oven and let sit for 10 minutes before eating.lace the chicken legs on the foil until the oven is preheated-about 15 minutes. When ready, put the pan in the oven and set your timer for 20 minutes.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to do chicken legs in a DC convection oven\\\"}\",\"answer\":\"Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to cook chicken legs in a DC convection oven:\\n\\n1. Combine seasonings and oil in a large glass baking dish, add the chicken legs and coat with the spice mixture. Cover and refrigerate overnight or for a few hours. (Passage 1)\\n2. Pre-heat the oven to Convection Roast or Convection Bake at 350 degrees. Place the chicken legs on a rimmed baking sheet and place it in the oven on rack position 2. Cook for 20 minutes, turn the 