e,\\\"upscale\\\":false},\\\"BusinessParking\\\":{\\\"garage\\\":false,\\\"lot\\\":false,\\\"street\\\":true,\\\"valet\\\":false,\\\"validated\\\":false},\\\"Music\\\":null,\\\"OutdoorSeating\\\":true,\\\"RestaurantsGoodForGroups\\\":true,\\\"RestaurantsReservations\\\":false,\\\"RestaurantsTakeOut\\\":null,\\\"WiFi\\\":\\\"no\\\"},\\\"business_stars\\\":4.5,\\\"categories\\\":\\\"Food, Restaurants, Delis, Event Planning & Services, Caterers, Sandwiches\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Santa Barbara\\\",\\\"hours\\\":{\\\"Friday\\\":\\\"10:30-15:0\\\",\\\"Monday\\\":\\\"10:30-15:0\\\",\\\"Saturday\\\":\\\"9:30-15:0\\\",\\\"Thursday\\\":\\\"10:30-15:0\\\",\\\"Tuesday\\\":\\\"10:30-15:0\\\",\\\"Wednesday\\\":\\\"10:30-15:0\\\"},\\\"name\\\":\\\"Three Pickles Subs and Sandwiches\\\",\\\"review_info\\\":[{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-12-15 22:39:52\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":4.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"I love pickles, so I definitely appreciate a pickles-forward sandwich shop. Three Pickles offers, true to its name, three varieties of pickles: spears, slices, and pepperoncini, all available gratis at a pickle bar, which is something I'd love to see wherever sandwiches are sold.\\\\n\\\\nWe met up with friends at the park the day before Thanksgiving and ordered sandwiches (and pickles) to pick up for a picnic lunch. Our friends ordered and we picked up, and both parts of the process seemed fast and easy enough.\\\\n\\\\nI ordered the house sub with Italian cold cuts. The \\\\\\\"sub our way\\\\\\\" came on a roll with diced tomato, onion, dill pickle, olive oil, oregano, mayo, choice of mustard, and choice of cheese, with a few optional add-ons. I picked dijon and provolone and added the pepperoncini and giardiniera (both free), as well as avocado. I got the regular size, which was smaller than I expected but plenty for one meal and about right for $9.50, though the $1.99 for the pitiable amount of avocado was a rip-off. The sandwich was good, if not especially exciting, and I enjoyed it with lots of pickled pepperoncini.\\\\n\\\\nI'd recommend Three Pickles if you're in the mood for a sandwich with lots of pickles. I am often in this mood, so I'll probably order from here again.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-12-03 20:39:41\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":3.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"The food's good but they way overcharge on DoorDash! $14.70 For a tiny sandwich and they didn't give me the pickle pack I ordered $3.50... never again.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-10-30 21:10:47\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":4.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Just looking for a quick sandwich late lunch. Went in around 2pm on a Saturday. Quick service, place looked very clean. Rubin sandwich was delicious! Would definitely go back.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\",\"answer\":\"Three Pickles Subs and Sandwiches is a food business located at 126 E Canon Perdido St in Santa Barbara, California. The business operates Monday through Friday from 10:30am to 5:00pm and Saturdays from 9:30am to 5:00pm. The categories associated with the business include Food, Restaurants, Delis, Event Planning & Services, Caterers, and Sandwiches. The business has a rating of 4.5 stars out of 5 on Google reviews.\\n\\nThe business has an outdoor seating area and is suitable for groups. WiFi is not available, and there are no reservations required for dining. Parking is available on the street, but not in a garage or lot.\\n\\nIn terms of food, the business specializes in sandwiches and pickles. There are three types of pickles available: spears, slices, and pepperoncini. These pickles can be purchased for free at a pickle bar. The business also offers a variety of sandwiches that can be customized with various toppings and add-ons. The prices for the sandwiches range from $8.50 to $11.50.\\n\\nThere are several positive reviews of the business on Google. One customer appreciated the variety of pickles available and found the sandwiches to be good, although they felt that the price for avocado was too high. Another customer noted that the food was good, but they were disappointed with the pricing on DoorDash. A third customer praised the quick service and cleanliness of the business and enjoyed their Rubin sandwich.\",\"source_segments\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":922},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":922,\"byte_end\":1261},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":1261,\"byte_end\":1409},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":1409,\"byte_end\":1579},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":1579,\"byte_end\":1684},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":1684,\"byte_end\":1860},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":1860,\"byte_end\":2053},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":2053,\"byte_end\":2244},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":2244,\"byte_end\":2330},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":2330,\"byte_end\":2462},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":2462,\"byte_end\":2496},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":2496,\"byte_end\":2536},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":2536,\"byte_end\":2566},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":2566,\"byte_end\":2608}],\"answer_sentence_indices\":[8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15],\"answer_offsets\":[{\"index\":0,\"byte_start\":0,\"byte_end\":117},{\"index\":1,\"byte_start\":117,\"byte_end\":221},{\"index\":2,\"byte_start\":221,\"byte_end\":352},{\"index\":3,\"byte_start\":352,\"byte_end\":420},{\"index\":4,\"byte_start\":420,\"byte_end\":489},{\"index\":5,\"byte_start\":489,\"byte_end\":563},{\"index\":6,\"byte_start\":563,\"byte_end\":628},{\"index\":7,\"byte_start\":628,\"byte_end\":698},{\"index\":8,\"byte_start\":698,\"byte_end\":776},{\"index\":9,\"byte_start\":776,\"byte_end\":833},{\"index\":10,\"byte_start\":833,\"byte_end\":940},{\"index\":11,\"byte_start\":940,\"byte_end\":999},{\"index\":12,\"byte_start\":999,\"byte_end\":1061},{\"index\":13,\"byte_start\":1061,\"byte_end\":1216},{\"index\":14,\"byte_start\":1216,\"byte_end\":1320},{\"index\":15,\"byte_start\":1320,\"byte_end\":1428}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
